<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William III, Duke of Aquitaine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 915–963</span> · Also known as William Towhead</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William III, Duke of Aquitaine, called Towhead, was count of Poitou from 935 and duke of Aquitaine from about 959 until his death in 963. Of the Ramnulfid family, he claimed the ducal title against the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> and Auvergne, and from his time the counts of Poitou were also dukes of Aquitaine. He retired to a monastery shortly before he died.</p></div>
